    <bpmn:process id="W_W248" name="W248. Store Inventory Variance &amp; LP Investigation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: High-value inventory variance flagged in cycle counts (W6) or annual physical count (W42)
Frequency: Ad-hoc (weekly reviews)
Volume: ~1–2 investigations per store/month (above-threshold variances per the LP canon)
Owner: Store Loss Prevention Officer
Participants: Store Manager, LP Auditor, Cashier Supervisor, WMS/ERP IT Specialist
Source: workflow W248 — Store Inventory Variance &amp; LP Investigation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W248_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W248_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W248_Lane2" name="LP Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W248_Lane3" name="LP Auditor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W248_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W248_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W248_Start6" name="High-value inventory variance flagged in cycle counts (W6) or annual physical count (W42)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W248_Task7" name="Alert Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Alert Generation: System auto-flags high-value SKU discrepancies (&gt; PHP 10,000 variance or &gt; 5% of bin stock) during count post-reconciliation (W6/W42).
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W248_Task8" name="Audit Trail Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Audit Trail Review: LP Officer extracts transactional audit logs for the flagged SKU: reviews receiving logs (W3/W18), transfer records (W22), POS sales details, and manual adjustment histories.
Responsible (R): LP Officer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W248_Task9" name="CCTV Timeline Correlation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CCTV Timeline Correlation: LP Officer maps count timestamp against CCTV footage using smart cameras with POS transaction overlay (W207); audits cash drawers for cashier scan errors.
Responsible (R): LP Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W248_Task10" name="Stock Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Stock Verification: LP team conducts a physical floor sweep and structural review of the adjacent bin locations to eliminate human putaway errors (W109).
Responsible (R): LP Auditor
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W248_Task11" name="Investigation Ruling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Investigation Ruling: LP Officer classifies the root cause: (a) Internal Theft / Shoplifting → triggers police/legal escalation; (b) Process Error (wrong SKU scanned at POS/GR) → triggers cashier/receiving retraining; (c) System Glitch → escalates to IT.
Responsible (R): LP Officer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W248_Task12" name="Adjustment Regularization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Adjustment Regularization: Store Manager authorizes stock correction journal in ERP per W92 adjustment guidelines to restore inventory count accuracy.
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W248_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W248_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W248_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W248_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Store Loss Prevention Officer review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Loss Prevention Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W248_Assoc15" sourceRef="W248_Annotation14" targetRef="W248_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
