    <bpmn:process id="W_W573" name="W573. Store-Level Daily Planogram Execution &amp; Shelf Compliance Check" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store opening (daily shelf walk); planogram update distribution from HQ
Frequency: Daily shelf walk at all 200 stores; planogram updates distributed as needed (typically weekly/bi-weekly)
Volume: ~200 daily compliance checks; focused checks on recently reset sections or promotional displays
Owner: Department Supervisor / Visual Merchandising Associate
Participants: Department Supervisor, Stock Associate, Store Manager (I), Visual Merchandising Associate (R for resets)
Source: workflow W573 — Store-Level Daily Planogram Execution &amp; Shelf Compliance Check</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W573_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W573_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W573_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W573_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W573_Start4" name="Store opening (daily shelf walk); planogram update distribution from HQ">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task5" name="Department Supervisor starts daily shelf walk using department planogram on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Department Supervisor starts daily shelf walk using department planogram on handheld device: at store opening (after initial replenishment by Stock Associates per W554), Department Supervisor logs into handheld and opens &quot;Daily Shelf Walk&quot; module; system loads assigned department planogram (4 departments per store: lumber/building, plumbing/electrical, tiles/flooring, tools/hardware); planogram displays aisle-by-aisle view with shelf positions; Supervisor selects starting aisle and begins walk
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task6" name="Walk first aisle of assigned department">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Walk first aisle of assigned department: Supervisor walks first aisle systematically: (a) start from aisle entrance end, (b) walk one side of aisle at eye-level, then return on opposite side, (c) scan 3–5 shelf positions per bay for visual compliance, (d) compare physical shelf layout to planogram image on handheld; for each aisle section, assess: facing quality, label accuracy, product placement correctness, shelf cleanliness, fixture condition
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–8 min per aisle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task7" name="Check product facing — pull forward items to shelf edge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Check product facing — pull forward items to shelf edge: for each SKU position: (a) verify at least one unit is pulled forward to the shelf edge lip (facing), (b) if product is pushed back beyond shelf edge: pull forward, (c) if facing quantity is less than planogram minimum front-facing count: flag for replenishment (links to W554 task list), (d) for heavy items (tile sample boards, paint cans, tool sets): ensure facing is stable and not at risk of falling; note: in hardware retail, &quot;facing&quot; is physically demanding — 20 kg paint cans and tile boxes cannot be easily repositioned one-handed
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min per bay</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task8" name="Verify shelf label matches product — flag mismatches for reprint">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Verify shelf label matches product — flag mismatches for reprint: for each SKU position: (a) verify shelf label product description matches physical product, (b) verify barcode on label matches product barcode (quick scan if uncertain), (c) verify price on label matches current system price (especially for promotional items), (d) if mismatch found: tap &quot;Label Mismatch&quot; on handheld — system generates label reprint task routed to W181 queue with priority; common mismatches: product placed in wrong position during replenishment, label from previous product not removed during reset, promotional price label not updated after promo ended
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 min per bay</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task9" name="Check promotional display positions against current planogram">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Check promotional display positions against current planogram: for promotional displays (endcaps, power aisle stacks, freestanding displays): (a) verify display matches current promotional planogram from W262, (b) verify promotional signage matches current promo (W13 promo calendar) — check promo dates have not expired, (c) verify promotional pricing is correct per W40 price file, (d) if promo has ended: flag for immediate teardown and restock to standard planogram, (e) if promo display is depleted: flag for replenishment or substitute facing
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min per display</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task10" name="Verify endcap and power aisle displays match HQ planogram template">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Verify endcap and power aisle displays match HQ planogram template: for permanent endcap positions and power aisle (main aisle) displays: (a) compare physical display to planogram template (MDM-023) on handheld, (b) verify correct products in correct positions per template, (c) verify display height and stack configuration matches template (safety consideration — unstable stacks of cement or tiles are a falling hazard), (d) take comparison photo for recently reset endcaps (within last 7 days) for Regional Manager review
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min per endcap</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task11" name="Report shelf damage or fixture issues to W47">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Report shelf damage or fixture issues to W47: during shelf walk, Supervisor identifies: (a) broken shelf brackets or sagging shelves (weight overload), (b) damaged peg hooks (bent, missing), (c) broken display fixtures, (d) damaged signage holders, (e) water damage to shelving units (especially in garden center and near loading dock); tap &quot;Report Damage&quot; on handheld: system auto-generates W47 facility maintenance work order with photo and location; priority based on safety risk (sagging shelf = high priority, cosmetic damage = normal queue)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 min per issue</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task12" name="For newly reset sections — detailed compliance check against updated planogram">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: For newly reset sections — detailed compliance check against updated planogram: for sections that were recently reset (planogram update applied within last 7 days): (a) perform detailed position-by-position compliance check against updated planogram, (b) photo documentation: take overview photo of full section + close-up photos of each shelf position, (c) compare each product position to planogram: correct product, correct position, correct facing quantity, correct label, (d) calculate compliance percentage for the reset section, (e) if compliance &lt; 90%: flag for corrective action within 24 hours by Stock Associate
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per reset section</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task13" name="Flag gaps where products are out-of-stock for extended periods">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Flag gaps where products are out-of-stock for extended periods: for SKU positions that are empty or have been at minimum facing for 3+ consecutive days: (a) check system for replenishment status (on order from DC, inter-store transfer pending, or discontinued), (b) if product is active but no replenishment in pipeline: escalate to Store Manager for manual order or substitute facing, (c) for substitute facing: apply W279 product substitution guidance — place a visually similar or related product in the gap with temporary label, (d) if product is discontinued: flag for planogram update request to HQ (MDM-023 change request)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 min per gap</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task14" name="Check price tag accuracy on promotional items">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Check price tag accuracy on promotional items: for items on current promotion (identified by promotional shelf tag or W13 promo calendar): (a) verify promotional price tag is displayed, (b) cross-reference promotional price with W40 price file on handheld, (c) verify promo dates on tag are current (not expired), (d) verify &quot;was/now&quot; pricing is accurate per DTI consumer protection requirements, (e) if discrepancy found: flag as price error per W553 pricing error workflow for immediate correction
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min per promotional section</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W573_Task15" name="Department Supervisor signs off daily shelf walk completion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Department Supervisor signs off daily shelf walk completion: after completing assigned department walk: (a) Supervisor reviews summary on handheld — total positions checked, exceptions found (label mismatches, facing issues, fixture damage, OOS gaps, promo discrepancies), (b) Supervisor adds notes on any unusual conditions, (c) signs off with electronic signature and timestamp, (d) system records completion and exception count per department per store per day
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W573_Task16" name="Weekly exception summary feeds into W86 monthly audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Weekly exception summary feeds into W86 monthly audit: system compiles daily shelf walk data into weekly summary: (a) total exceptions by category (labels, facing, fixtures, OOS, promo), (b) trend by department (improving or deteriorating), (c) exception resolution rate (what % of flagged items were resolved within 24 hours), (d) repeat exception locations (same position flagged 3+ days in a row); weekly summary feeds into W86 monthly planogram compliance audit as: (a) pre-audit focus areas (departments with highest exception rates get priority audit attention), (b) historical compliance trend data, (c) exception resolution effectiveness metric
Responsible (R): System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated (weekly summary generation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W573_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W573_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W573_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W573_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Stock Associate (W554) handling heavy item facing during replenishment and Supervisor focusing on visual compliance check rather than physical repositioning; operational: separate yard display guidelines (visual placement standards rather than fixed planogram positions) and W554 Step 9 yard restacking protocol; operational: HQ distributing updated planograms 3 days before effective date via W571 communication
Owner: Department Supervisor / Visual Merchandising Associate</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W573_Assoc19" sourceRef="W573_Annotation18" targetRef="W573_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
