    <bpmn:process id="W_W723" name="W723. Store-Level Loading Bay Traffic &amp; Truck Queue Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled delivery truck arrival; or DSD vendor truck arrival per W18B
Frequency: 2–3 replenishment trucks per store per week (DC) + ~2–3 DSD trucks per store per month
Volume: ~80–120 truck arrivals/day chain-wide (DC ~400–600/week + DSD ~500–600/month + transfers and return pickups)
Owner: Receiving Clerk
Participants: Receiving Clerk, Stock Associate, Truck Driver, Security Guard
Source: workflow W723 — Store-Level Loading Bay Traffic &amp; Truck Queue Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W723_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W723_Lane1" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W723_Lane2" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W723_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W723_Start4" name="Scheduled delivery truck arrival; or DSD vendor truck arrival per W18B">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W723_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W723_Task5" name="Daily delivery schedule review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily delivery schedule review: at start of day, Receiving Clerk reviews delivery schedule: (a) system displays expected deliveries: DC replenishment trucks (from W4 transfer orders), DSD vendor trucks (from W18B scheduled deliveries), inter-store transfers (from W22), return pickups (from W22B); (b) note expected arrival time windows and number of pallets/cases per truck; (c) identify potential conflicts: multiple trucks scheduled in same time window; (d) adjust receiving sequence if needed: prioritize perishable/temperature-sensitive items, time-critical promotional stock per W57; (e) communicate adjusted schedule to Security Guard for gate coordination
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10-15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W723_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W723_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W723_Task6" name="Truck arrival and queuing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Truck arrival and queuing: when truck arrives: (a) Security Guard directs truck to loading bay or queue area: (i) if loading bay available: direct to bay; (ii) if loading bay occupied: direct to queue area and assign queue position; (iii) if customer vehicles in yard loading area per W438: prioritize customer safety, hold truck until yard is clear; (b) Security Guard verifies truck identity: driver matches scheduled delivery, license plate matches expected vehicle; (c) for unscheduled/unexpected trucks: Receiving Clerk verifies against open POs or transfer orders before accepting; refuse delivery if no matching order
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min per truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W723_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W723_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W723_Task7" name="Bay allocation and turnaround management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Bay allocation and turnaround management: Receiving Clerk manages bay turnaround: (a) target turnaround time: DC replenishment trucks = 45-60 min; DSD trucks = 20-30 min; inter-store transfers = 30-45 min; (b) monitor receiving progress: if truck exceeding target turnaround, investigate bottleneck (missing PO, product discrepancy, short-staffed); (c) if queue is building (2+ trucks waiting): (i) request additional Stock Associate support; (ii) expedite current truck completion; (iii) communicate wait time to queued drivers; (d) for DSD vendors: enforce W18B delivery time window compliance; late arrivals may be rescheduled
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W723_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W723_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W723_Task8" name="Customer yard conflict management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer yard conflict management: loading bay area also serves customer yard loading per W438: (a) separate customer loading zone from commercial truck bay with clear signage and barriers; (b) if customer loading blocks truck access: Security Guard assists with customer vehicle relocation; (c) if commercial truck blocks customer access: expedite truck departure or redirect to alternate bay; (d) ensure pedestrian safety: customers walking through yard area are separated from forklift and truck traffic by barriers and signage
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W723_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W723_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W723_Task9" name="Daily bay utilization reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Daily bay utilization reporting: at end of day: (a) system generates daily loading bay utilization report: number of trucks received, average turnaround time, peak hour utilization, queue wait times, customer vs. truck conflict incidents; (b) Receiving Clerk reviews for anomalies; (c) report feeds into weekly store operations review per W575; (d) persistent queuing issues escalated to Regional Manager for DC delivery schedule adjustment or facility improvement
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5-10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W723_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W723_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W723_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W723_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W723_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: physical separation and dedicated customer loading zone
Owner: Receiving Clerk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W723_Assoc12" sourceRef="W723_Annotation11" targetRef="W723_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
