    <bpmn:process id="W_W771" name="W771. Store-Level BOPIS Order Aging &amp; Abandoned Pickup Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BOPIS order exceeds 5-day hold period without customer pickup
Frequency: Daily; ~200–300 abandoned BOPIS orders per week chain-wide
Volume: ~200–300 aged BOPIS orders/week across 200 stores (~1–2 per store per week)
Owner: Customer Service Rep
Participants: Customer Service Rep, Stock Associate, Store Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W771 — Store-Level BOPIS Order Aging &amp; Abandoned Pickup Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W771_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W771_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W771_Lane2" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W771_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W771_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W771_Lane5" name="CX Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W771_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W771_Start7" name="BOPIS order exceeds 5-day hold period without customer pickup">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W771_Task8" name="Daily aging report review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily aging report review: System generates BOPIS order aging report: (a) Day 3 orders — automated reminder notification to customer via W708 (SMS, email, app push), (b) Day 4 orders — CSR makes personal phone call to customer, (c) Day 5 orders — final notification and pickup deadline (store closing time)
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W771_Task9" name="Day 3 automated reminder">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Day 3 automated reminder: System sends pickup reminder: &quot;Your BuildRight order #[X] is ready for pickup at [Store Name]. Please pick up by [Date/Time] or your order will be cancelled and refunded.&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W771_Task10" name="Day 4 personal outreach">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Day 4 personal outreach: CSR calls customer: (a) confirms customer received notifications, (b) offers pickup extension (maximum 2 additional days per Store Manager approval), (c) if customer wants to cancel — process cancellation per W98 with auto-refund, (d) log outcome in order management system
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/call</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W771_Task11" name="Day 5 abandoned order processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Day 5 abandoned order processing: For orders not picked up by store closing on Day 5: (a) system auto-cancels order per W536 unified order management, (b) inventory returned to saleable stock — system removes hold and updates ATP across all channels, (c) automated refund initiated per original payment method via W101
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W771_Task12" name="Customer cancellation notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer cancellation notification: System sends cancellation notification: &quot;Your order #[X] has been cancelled as it was not picked up within 5 days. A refund of PHP [X] has been processed to your [payment method]. Please allow 3-5 business days for the refund to appear.&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W771_Task13" name="Staged inventory restock">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Staged inventory restock: Stock Associate returns staged items from BOPIS staging area to selling floor: (a) verify item condition, (b) return to shelf location per planogram (W86), (c) system confirms inventory is available for sale
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W771_Task14" name="Weekly BOPIS abandonment analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Weekly BOPIS abandonment analytics: Store Manager reviews weekly abandonment metrics: (a) abandonment rate by store, (b) customer response to Day 3/4 outreach, (c) refund processing accuracy, (d) inventory restock timeliness; feeds to W575 weekly operations review
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W771_Task15" name="Monthly chain-wide BOPIS optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly chain-wide BOPIS optimization: Monthly: ecommerce and CX teams review chain-wide BOPIS abandonment patterns: (a) stores with &gt; 5% abandonment rate root cause analysis, (b) seasonal or product-category correlation, (c) customer feedback from abandoned orders, (d) recommendations for pickup SLA or communication improvements
Responsible (R): CX Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W771_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W771_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W771_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W771_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Customer Service Rep review and approval gate
Owner: Customer Service Rep</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
