    <bpmn:process id="W_W824" name="W824. Store-Level Lumber Yard &amp; Outdoor Area Daily Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store opening per W5A; daily operational cycle for outdoor/lumber yard areas
Frequency: Daily; 200 stores with lumber yards
Volume: 200 stores x daily operations; each store has 500-2,000 sqm outdoor yard area
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Receiving Clerk, Stock Associate, Sales Associate, Yard Helper
Source: workflow W824 — Store-Level Lumber Yard &amp; Outdoor Area Daily Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W824_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W824_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W824_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W824_Lane3" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W824_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W824_Start5" name="Store opening per W5A; daily operational cycle for outdoor/lumber yard areas">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W824_Task6" name="Morning yard inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning yard inspection: Department Supervisor conducts pre-opening walkthrough: (a) check overnight security — gate locks, CCTV per W71 physical security, fencing integrity, no signs of unauthorized entry, (b) inspect material stacks for weather damage (rain-soaked cement bags, warped lumber, rust on steel rebar), (c) verify forklift pre-operation check per W579 daily equipment safety — fluid levels, tire condition, horn/lights, (d) check safety signage and barriers in place (hard hat zone, forklift zone, pedestrian walkway), (e) verify catch-weight scale calibration per W463 — test weigh a known reference
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W824_Task7" name="Material display and restocking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material display and restocking: Stock Associate organizes lumber racks and building material displays: (a) replenish from backstock per W554 daily restocking — priority items: cement, hollow blocks, lumber, plywood, (b) ensure price tags displayed per W667 price verification — outdoor weatherproof tags, (c) sort lumber by species and dimension (tanguile, narra, mahogany; 2x2, 2x3, 2x4, 2x6), (d) stack cement bags properly — max 10 bags high per safety, on pallets to prevent moisture wicking from ground, (e) arrange hollow blocks for easy customer access — stable stacks, no leaning towers
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30-60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W824_Task8" name="Customer service operations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer service operations: Sales Associate assists yard customers: (a) material selection and quantity estimation per W823 — &quot;How many hollow blocks for a 10-meter perimeter wall, 2 meters high?&quot;, (b) catch-weight processing for lumber and wire per W463 — measure and weigh on yard scale, (c) cutting services for lumber and pipe per W169 — cross-cut and rip-cut to customer specifications, (d) loading coordination per W438 yard dispatch — assist customer vehicle loading safely
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Integrated into selling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W824_Task9" name="Weather monitoring and protection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Weather monitoring and protection: Department Supervisor monitors weather conditions throughout the day: (a) if rain approaching: cover exposed materials immediately — tarp over cement bags, plywood, MDF, insulation; roll up lumber end-grain protectors, (b) if PAGASA typhoon signal raised for store area: activate W576 severe weather protocol — secure all outdoor materials, suspend yard operations, protect equipment, (c) post-wet weather: inspect for water damage — test cement bags for hardening (lump test), check plywood for delamination, process damaged goods per W91 for markdown or disposal
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15-30 min as needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W824_Task10" name="Yard safety management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Yard safety management: (a) enforce PPE requirements for yard staff per W780 — hard hats, steel-toe boots, high-visibility vests mandatory in yard, (b) manage forklift traffic — pedestrian exclusion zones clearly marked, forklift horn when turning corners, speed limit 5 kph in customer areas, (c) customer loading safety per W438 — only trained staff operate forklift/hoist for loading customer vehicles, customers must stand clear during loading, (d) daily hazard check per W559 — tripping hazards (loose lumber offcuts, stray nails), unstable stacks, loose materials, standing water after rain
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Ongoing throughout day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W824_Task11" name="End-of-day yard close">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: End-of-day yard close: (a) secure all gates and access points — chain and padlock main yard gate, verify CCTV coverage active per W71, (b) cover exposed materials — cement bags, plywood, insulation, (c) forklift parked and locked per safety protocol — key removed, parked in designated area, parking brake engaged, (d) yard inventory spot-check for high-value items — steel bars, premium lumber (narra, mahogany), expensive hardware (galvanized sheets), (e) report any losses, damages, or safety incidents to Store Manager via daily yard operations log
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W824_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W824_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W824_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W824_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: exclusion zones but enforcement is difficult during peak hours
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W824_Assoc14" sourceRef="W824_Annotation13" targetRef="W824_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow15" sourceRef="W824_Start5" targetRef="W824_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow16" sourceRef="W824_Task6" targetRef="W824_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow17" sourceRef="W824_Task7" targetRef="W824_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow18" sourceRef="W824_Task8" targetRef="W824_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow19" sourceRef="W824_Task9" targetRef="W824_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow20" sourceRef="W824_Task10" targetRef="W824_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W824_Flow21" sourceRef="W824_Task11" targetRef="W824_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
