    <bpmn:process id="W_W1028" name="W1028. Store-Level Shopping Cart, Basket &amp; Customer Equipment Inventory Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly scheduled inventory count; also triggered by customer complaint about unavailable carts
Frequency: Weekly count × 200 stores; monthly condition assessment
Volume: ~80–120 shopping carts and ~50–80 hand baskets per store
Owner: Assistant Store Manager
Participants: Customer Service Rep, Maintenance/Utility Staff
Source: workflow W1028 — Store-Level Shopping Cart, Basket &amp; Customer Equipment Inventory Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1028_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1028_Lane1" name="Customer Service Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1028_Lane2" name="Maintenance Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1028_Lane3" name="Assistant Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1028_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1028_Start5" name="Weekly scheduled inventory count; also triggered by customer complaint about unavailable…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1028_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1028_Task6" name="Weekly Cart &amp; Basket Count">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly Cart &amp; Basket Count: Customer Service Rep conducts weekly count: (a) count all carts and baskets physically present in store: cart corrals (parking lot), store entrance, lumber yard, backroom staging area; (b) compare against system inventory (expected count); (c) if actual &lt; expected by more than 5%: initiate cart retrieval — walk parking lot perimeter, adjacent lots, and nearby sidewalks; (d) recovered carts returned to corral; (e) unrecovered carts (missing &gt; 7 days) written off in system; (f) if actual &lt; minimum threshold (80 shopping carts, 40 baskets), immediately order replacements from vendor per W136 (indirect procurement); (g) system logs count with variance and retrieval results
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1028_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1028_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1028_Task7" name="Monthly Condition Assessment &amp; Repair Triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly Condition Assessment &amp; Repair Triage: Maintenance/Utility Staff conducts monthly condition check: (a) inspect each cart and basket: wheel function (swivel, no wobble, no flat spots on solid tires), frame integrity (no bends, cracks, or rust-through), handle grip condition, child seat/strap function (for carts with child seats), basket cleanliness, store branding/logo condition; (b) categorize: Serviceable (no action), Minor Repair (wheel replacement, grip replacement, strap replacement — completed in-house), Major Repair (frame weld, structural — sent to vendor or scrapped), Retire (beyond economical repair); (c) minor repairs completed same day using on-hand spare parts (wheels, grips, straps); (d) major repairs queued for vendor pickup or scrapped; (e) retired carts/baskets removed from system inventory and dispositioned per W502 (non-hazardous waste) or W443 (scrap metal revenue); (f) generate replacement order if net available count falls below minimum threshold
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1028_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1028_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1028_Task8" name="Cart Corral &amp; Parking Lot Retrieval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cart Corral &amp; Parking Lot Retrieval: Daily (during peak hours): (a) Customer Service Rep or designated cart retrieval staff walks parking lot every 2 hours during peak times (10AM–2PM, 4PM–7PM); (b) returns stray carts from parking spaces, adjacent lots, and sidewalk areas to corrals; (c) corrals organized: shopping carts in main corral, flatbed and lumber carts at designated staging near lumber yard exit; (d) special attention during rainy season — carts left in parking lot accumulate water and rust faster; (e) Customer Service Rep monitors cart availability at entrance during peak — if &lt; 20% of carts available, trigger immediate parking lot retrieval round
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per round (3–4 rounds/day)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1028_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1028_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1028_Task9" name="Replacement Procurement &amp; Asset Registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Replacement Procurement &amp; Asset Registration: When replacements are needed: (a) Assistant Store Manager creates purchase request in system per W136 (indirect procurement) specifying type, quantity, and specification; (b) standard BuildRight cart specification: heavy-duty steel frame, powder-coated (anti-corrosion for Philippine humidity), 100 kg load capacity, 4 swivel wheels (2 locking), child seat with 5-point harness, BuildRight branding; (c) upon receipt, Maintenance Staff assembles (if knock-down) and registers each cart/basket in asset tracking module with unique barcode tag; (d) barcode tag affixed to cart frame — scanned during weekly count for tracking; (e) capitalization: individual carts below PHP 5,000 are expensed as consumables; flatbed carts and platform trucks above PHP 5,000 capitalized as fixed assets per W39
Responsible (R): Assistant Store Manager / Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per procurement event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1028_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1028_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1028_Task10" name="Customer Feedback &amp; Continuous Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer Feedback &amp; Continuous Improvement: (a) if customer complains about cart/basket unavailability during shopping trip, Customer Service Rep logs complaint in system per W41; (b) if more than 3 cart unavailability complaints per week, trigger emergency procurement; (c) annually: review cart/basket-to-customer ratio — benchmark 1 cart per 15 peak-hour customers; (d) evaluate new cart designs: anti-theft wheel locks (cart won&#x27;t roll beyond parking lot perimeter via embedded RFID), ergonomic designs, branded carts as marketing touchpoint
Responsible (R): Assistant Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1028_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1028_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1028_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1028_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1028_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Assistant Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Assistant Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1028_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1028_Annotation12" targetRef="W1028_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
