    <bpmn:process id="W_W1037" name="W1037. Store-Level Annual Physical Inventory Preparation, Execution &amp; Variance Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual scheduled physical inventory date (typically January–February, post-holiday, pre-peak season)
Frequency: Annual per store; each store completes physical inventory within a single day
Volume: 35,000 SKUs × 200 stores; each store counts all inventory in a single 10–14 hour event
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: All Store Staff (29), District Manager (supervision), LP Officer (observation), Internal Audit (W342 observation), Finance Controller (variance approval)
Source: workflow W1037 — Store-Level Annual Physical Inventory Preparation, Execution &amp; Variance Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1037_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1037_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1037_Lane2" name="All Store Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1037_Lane3" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1037_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1037_Start5" name="Annual scheduled physical inventory date (typically January–February, post-holiday…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1037_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1037_Task6" name="Pre-Count Preparation (2 weeks before)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-Count Preparation (2 weeks before): Store Manager begins preparation: (a) Housekeeping: all merchandise on correct shelves per planogram (W573); no items on floor without designated location; backroom organized — all items on shelves, not on pallets; (b) Receiving cut-off: all pending goods receipts (W109) and returns (W12) processed and posted to system before count day — no unprocessed GRs or returns in backroom; (c) RTV consolidation: all RTV-eligible items shipped to DC per W1035 before count day — no RTV items in quarantine; (d) Damaged goods disposition: all damaged items processed per W91 before count day — no damaged items in active inventory; (e) Count team assignment: Store Manager assigns counting teams (2-person teams: 1 counter + 1 recorder): 8–10 teams for selling floor, 2 teams for backroom, 1 team for lumber yard/outdoor area; (f) Equipment preparation: charge all RF guns and tablets, print count sheets for backup, prepare labels for counted areas, test barcode scanners; (g) Pre-count report: system generates expected inventory report by location for reconciliation during count
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 hours (spread over 2 weeks)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1037_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1037_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1037_Task7" name="Count Day Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Count Day Execution: Store closed to public on count day (typically a Tuesday–Thursday for lowest customer impact): (a) Opening briefing (6:00 AM): Store Manager briefs all staff on count procedures, team assignments, area boundaries, and rules: (i) count everything — do not skip any location, (ii) count by scanning barcode (RF gun) — not by visual estimation, (iii) for bulk items (cement bags, nails by kg, lumber by board foot): count each unit individually, (iv) for catch-weight items (nails in bulk bins): weigh on scale and convert to units per W463, (v) record exactly what is physically present — do not adjust to match system quantity; (b) Area-by-area counting (6:30 AM – 4:00 PM): teams count assigned areas; each area sealed with &quot;COUNTED&quot; tape upon completion; team leader performs blind recount of 10% of items for quality check; (c) Running variance check: as each section is completed, system compares count vs. system quantity in real-time; sections with variance &gt; 3% flagged for immediate recount by different team; (d) Lunch rotation: teams rotate lunch breaks to maintain continuous counting; (e) Progress tracking: Store Manager monitors count completion on dashboard — which areas completed, which in progress, which not started
Responsible (R): All Store Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–14 hours (6 AM – 8 PM)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1037_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1037_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1037_Task8" name="Variance Analysis &amp; Recount">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Variance Analysis &amp; Recount: After initial count completion: (a) system generates variance report: SKU, location, system qty, count qty, variance (units and value); (b) Store Manager and Department Supervisors review high-value variances: (i) items with variance &gt; PHP 10,000 in value: mandatory recount by DM or LP Officer; (ii) items with variance &gt; 5% of system qty: recount by different team; (iii) zero-count items where system shows stock: investigate — is item misplaced, stolen, or mislabeled? (c) recount results entered in system; if recount confirms original count, variance stands; if recount differs, third count by Store Manager personally; (d) all recounts documented with team members, timestamp, and result
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors / Store Manager / DM / LP Officer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1037_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1037_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1037_Task9" name="Variance Approval &amp; System Adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Variance Approval &amp; System Adjustment: (a) Store Manager compiles final variance summary: total positive variance (overage), total negative variance (shortage), net variance by department, net variance by category; (b) Shrinkage calculation: net negative variance (shortage) as % of total system inventory value — this is the store&#x27;s annual shrinkage rate; compare against target of &lt; 1.5% per model company profile; (c) Store Manager submits variance report to Finance Controller with explanation for material variances; (d) Finance Controller reviews: (i) variance within normal range (&lt; 1.5% shrinkage): approve adjustment; (ii) variance exceeds threshold (&gt; 1.5% shrinkage): escalate to Internal Audit per W342 for investigation before approval; (iii) significant positive variance (overage &gt; 0.5%): investigate — possible receiving errors or unrecorded inter-store transfers; (e) upon approval: system posts inventory adjustment per W92 with appropriate GL entries; (f) LP Officer incorporates physical inventory results into annual shrinkage analysis per W845
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–4 hours (Finance review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1037_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1037_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1037_Task10" name="Post-Count Lessons Learned &amp; Process Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-Count Lessons Learned &amp; Process Improvement: Within 1 week after physical inventory: (a) Store Manager conducts debrief with all counting teams: what went well, what caused delays, which areas were problematic; (b) DM conducts post-count review with Store Manager: (i) compare this store&#x27;s shrinkage rate vs. district average and chain average; (ii) identify departments with highest shrinkage for targeted LP intervention per W845; (iii) evaluate count efficiency: hours to complete, recount rate, accuracy of first count; (c) Finance team compiles chain-wide physical inventory summary: (i) total chain shrinkage rate, (ii) shrinkage by region, by store, by category, (iii) year-over-year trend, (iv) financial impact: total inventory write-off value; (d) recommendations fed into: (i) loss prevention program per W846, (ii) cycle counting program adjustments per W6 (increase frequency in high-shrinkage areas), (iii) receiving process improvements per W666, (iv) store staffing adequacy per model company staffing model (29 per store)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DM / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 hours per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1037_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1037_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1037_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1037_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1037_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1037_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1037_Annotation12" targetRef="W1037_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1037_Flow14" sourceRef="W1037_Start5" targetRef="W1037_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1037_Flow15" sourceRef="W1037_Task6" targetRef="W1037_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1037_Flow16" sourceRef="W1037_Task7" targetRef="W1037_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1037_Flow17" sourceRef="W1037_Task8" targetRef="W1037_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1037_Flow18" sourceRef="W1037_Task9" targetRef="W1037_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1037_Flow19" sourceRef="W1037_Task10" targetRef="W1037_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1037_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1037_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1037">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1037_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1037_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
