    <bpmn:process id="W_W1112" name="W1112. Store-Level Inventory Age-Based Auto-Markdown &amp; Clearance Trigger" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Nightly batch job (inventory aging report), or manual review triggered by category manager
Frequency: Nightly (automated batch); weekly review by Department Supervisor
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs × 200 stores = 7,000,000 SKU-location combinations checked nightly
Owner: Department Supervisor (store-level execution)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Stock Associate, Store Manager, Category Manager (pricing approval)
Source: workflow W1112 — Store-Level Inventory Age-Based Auto-Markdown &amp; Clearance Trigger</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1112_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1112_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1112_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1112_Start3" name="Nightly batch job (inventory aging report), or manual review triggered by category manager">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1112_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1112_Task4" name="Nightly Inventory Aging Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Nightly Inventory Aging Analysis: (a) nightly batch job runs against all inventory records: for each SKU at each location, calculates days since last receipt (age of oldest unit in stock), days since last sale (sell-through velocity), and total on-hand quantity; (b) system classifies each SKU-location into aging buckets: Fresh (0–60 days) — no action; Maturing (61–90 days) — monitor list; Aging (91–120 days) — 1st markdown trigger; Old (121–180 days) — 2nd markdown trigger; Stale (181–270 days) — 3rd markdown trigger; Dead (271+ days) — clearance/write-off trigger; (c) system adjusts thresholds by ABC class: A-items (fast movers) trigger markdowns earlier (60/90/120/150/180 days), C-items (slow movers) get longer grace periods (120/180/270/360/400 days); (d) seasonal items have separate aging profiles based on seasonal calendar (W306) — e.g., Christmas items that age past January 15 trigger accelerated markdown regardless of standard thresholds
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): automated
Duration: nightly batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1112_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1112_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1112_Task5" name="Auto-Markdown Calculation &amp; Notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Auto-Markdown Calculation &amp; Notification: (a) for items triggering a markdown threshold, system calculates new price: (i) 1st markdown (Aging): 15% off current price; (ii) 2nd markdown (Old): 30% off current price; (iii) 3rd markdown (Stale): 50% off current price; (iv) Dead: 70% off or write-off (if below cost); (b) system generates daily markdown notification list per store, distributed to Department Supervisor&#x27;s tablet and Store Manager&#x27;s dashboard; (c) list includes: item description, current price, proposed markdown price, markdown %, current on-hand, days since last sale, and estimated markdown value impact; (d) Department Supervisor reviews the list: (i) approve — system auto-updates price; (ii) defer — item placed on 7-day hold with reason code (e.g., &quot;seasonal item expected to sell in upcoming promotion&quot;); (iii) escalate to Category Manager — for items where markdown may conflict with upcoming vendor-funded promotions (W513) or contractual minimum price requirements
Responsible (R): System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor (≤ 30% markdown); Store Manager (&gt; 30% markdown)
Duration: 15–30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1112_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1112_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1112_Task6" name="Price Update Execution &amp; Shelf Label Reprint">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Price Update Execution &amp; Shelf Label Reprint: (a) upon approval, system updates the item&#x27;s price in the pricing master for that store location; (b) system generates shelf label reprint batch for all approved markdown items; (c) Stock Associate prints new shelf labels from store label printer and replaces old labels on shelf; (d) POS system automatically picks up new prices (real-time event streaming per W533); (e) markdown items tagged with clearance flag in POS — visible on receipt as &quot;CLEARANCE — No Returns&quot; per W532 (clearance &amp; final sale processing); (f) system tracks markdown items on e-commerce catalog with updated pricing and &quot;Clearance&quot; badge
Responsible (R): System / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–30 min/day for label updates</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1112_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1112_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1112_Task7" name="Clearance Event Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Clearance Event Coordination: (a) when items reach the &quot;Stale&quot; or &quot;Dead&quot; bucket across multiple stores, system aggregates and recommends a coordinated clearance event: (i) if ≥ 5 stores have the same SKU in Stale/Dead status, system proposes a &quot;Chain-Wide Clearance&quot; promotion; (ii) Category Manager reviews and approves chain-wide clearance pricing; (iii) Marketing notified for promotional signage and social media announcement (W83); (b) for items in &quot;Dead&quot; status with quantity &lt; 5 units across the chain, system recommends: (i) consolidation to a single store via inter-store transfer (W22) for efficient clearance, or (ii) write-off and disposition per W91 (damaged goods) if below recovery threshold
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1112_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1112_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1112_Task8" name="Monthly Markdown Effectiveness Report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Markdown Effectiveness Report: (a) system generates monthly markdown effectiveness report: (i) total markdown value by aging bucket, category, and store; (ii) sell-through rate post-markdown (target: ≥ 60% of markdown units sold within 30 days); (iii) recovery rate: markdown revenue / original inventory cost; (iv) items requiring multiple markdown rounds (indicating initial markdown was insufficient); (v) dead stock write-off value; (b) report informs Category Manager&#x27;s assortment rationalization decisions (W679) and buyer replenishment parameter tuning; (c) financial provision for markdown liability adjusted in GL per W220 (SLOB provisioning)
Responsible (R): System / Finance
Accountable (A): Category Manager / CFO
Duration: automated monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1112_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1112_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1112_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1112_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1112_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (store-level execution) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (store-level execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1112_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1112_Annotation10" targetRef="W1112_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
