    <bpmn:process id="W_W1123" name="W1123. Store-Level Customer Project Progress Site Visit &amp; Material Delivery Verification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer request for on-site verification of delivered materials, or scheduled milestone visit for large B2B/project accounts
Frequency: ~500–800 site visits/month across all stores (primarily for project/trade accounts)
Volume: 1 visit per request; ~2–4 visits per active project account
Owner: Department Supervisor (or Sales Associate designated as project liaison)
Participants: Department Supervisor / Sales Associate (Project Liaison), Customer, Delivery Partner
Source: workflow W1123 — Store-Level Customer Project Progress Site Visit &amp; Material Delivery Verification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1123_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1123_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1123_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1123_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1123_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1123_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1123_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1123_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1123_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1123_Start4" name="Customer request for on-site verification of delivered materials, or scheduled milestone…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1123_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1123_Task5" name="Visit Scheduling &amp; Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Visit Scheduling &amp; Preparation: (a) project liaison reviews active project accounts with upcoming or recent deliveries; (b) schedules site visit within 24–48 hours of material delivery; (c) prepares site visit checklist from ERP: PO details, delivery manifest, material specifications, batch/shade numbers for tiles, grade markings for lumber; (d) coordinates with customer site contact for access and safety orientation; (e) brings mobile tablet with ERP access and camera for documentation
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Project Liaison)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1123_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1123_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1123_Task6" name="On-Site Material Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: On-Site Material Verification: (a) verify delivered quantities against PO and delivery receipt: count bags of cement, bundles of rebar, boxes of tiles, sheets of plywood; (b) check specifications: tile shade/batch code matches order (photograph shade lot number), lumber grade stamp visible and correct, rebar diameter and grade verified, cement brand and type correct; (c) inspect condition: no broken tiles, no water-damaged cement bags, no warped lumber, no corroded roofing sheets; (d) verify on-site storage: materials elevated on pallets, covered if outdoors, cement kept dry; (e) document any discrepancies with photos and notes in ERP mobile app
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Project Liaison)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1123_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1123_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1123_Task7" name="Discrepancy Resolution &amp; Replacement Order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Discrepancy Resolution &amp; Replacement Order: (a) if discrepancies found: short shipment, wrong item, or damage — immediately initiate replacement PO from mobile app; (b) system creates replacement order with priority flag for next available delivery slot; (c) credit note generated for damaged/incorrect items per W101; (d) customer signs digital acknowledgment of verified quantities and condition; (e) if no discrepancies, customer confirms receipt and satisfaction in system
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Project Liaison) / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1123_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1123_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1123_Task8" name="Visit Report &amp; Follow-Up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Visit Report &amp; Follow-Up: (a) system auto-generates site visit report with photos, verification checklist, and any issues; (b) report emailed to customer and stored in project account record; (c) project liaison schedules next milestone visit or confirms project on track; (d) any quality issues flagged for vendor feedback per W110 (supplier quality CAPA)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1123_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1123_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1123_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1123_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1123_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (or Sales Associate designated as project liaison) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (or Sales Associate designated as project liaison)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
