    <bpmn:process id="W_W1139" name="W1139. Store-Level Lumber Yard Inventory Seasonal Rotation &amp; Grade Segregation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly inventory review, or seasonal merchandise transition (W264), or significant lumber delivery receipt
Frequency: Quarterly full rotation; ongoing daily segregation during receiving
Volume: ~4,900 lumber &amp; building material SKUs per store; ~200–300 items requiring seasonal rotation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Stock Associate (Lumber Yard), Department Supervisor, Receiving Clerk
Source: workflow W1139 — Store-Level Lumber Yard Inventory Seasonal Rotation &amp; Grade Segregation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1139_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1139_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1139_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1139_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1139_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1139_Lane2" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1139_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1139_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1139_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1139_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1139_Start5" name="Quarterly inventory review, or seasonal merchandise transition (W264), or significant…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1139_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1139_Task6" name="Quarterly Seasonal Yard Reorganization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly Seasonal Yard Reorganization: (a) before each quarter, Department Supervisor reviews seasonal demand forecast for lumber &amp; building materials; (b) dry season (Dec–May plan): position dimensional lumber (2×2, 2×3, 2×4, 2×6), plywood (1/4&quot;, 3/8&quot;, 1/2&quot;, 3/4&quot;), GI roofing sheets, cement, and rebar in front-of-yard accessible positions; (c) rainy season (Jun–Nov plan): move indoor renovation materials (moldings, doors, pre-finished panels) to more accessible positions; reduce outdoor lumber front-stocking to minimum display quantities; (d) update yard layout map in ERP for receiving clerk guidance; (e) seasonal reorganization typically requires 2–3 stock associates for 4–6 hours
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Stock Associates
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours (quarterly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1139_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1139_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1139_Task7" name="Grade Segregation During Receiving">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Grade Segregation During Receiving: (a) when lumber delivery arrives, Receiving Clerk checks grade stamp on each bundle: Philippine lumber grades (if locally sourced) or international grades (if imported — e.g., SPF from Canada, Radiata Pine from New Zealand); (b) bundles sorted by grade into designated yard sections: Premium/Select grade — covered area, customer-facing display; Common #1/Construction grade — main yard stacks; Common #2/Utility grade — rear yard, clearance section; (c) each stack labeled with: species, grade, dimension, treatment status (treated vs. untreated), and price per board foot/piece; (d) grade discrepancies flagged: if bundle contains mixed grades, segregate and relabel
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1139_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1139_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1139_Task8" name="Daily Grade Integrity Spot Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Daily Grade Integrity Spot Check: (a) during morning yard walkthrough, Stock Associate checks that: grade labels are visible and accurate on all stacks; customer picks haven&#x27;t mixed grades (customer took from wrong stack); moisture-damaged pieces are not mixed with sound stock; (b) any mixed-grade stacks re-sorted immediately; (c) grade labels replaced if damaged by weather or handling
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1139_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1139_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1139_Task9" name="Inventory Valuation Accuracy Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inventory Valuation Accuracy Audit: (a) quarterly: Department Supervisor verifies that ERP inventory matches physical grade distribution; (b) system reports lumber inventory by grade with weighted average cost per grade; (c) physical count of sample stacks compared to ERP quantities; (d) discrepancies investigated per W514 (variance root cause analysis); (e) grade-specific valuation: Select grade valued higher than Utility — if ERP doesn&#x27;t distinguish grades, inventory may be misvalued
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours (quarterly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1139_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1139_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1139_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1139_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1139_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
