    <bpmn:process id="W_W1193" name="W1193. Heavy &amp; Bulky Material Customer Pickup Scheduling &amp; Loading Bay Priority Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases heavy/bulky items (cement, lumber, plywood, tiles, steel, sand/gravel) and selects &quot;Customer Pickup&quot; at POS or online
Frequency: ~40–60 customer pickups/store/week (200 stores = ~8,000–12,000/week chain-wide)
Volume: ~2–3% of store transactions involve a scheduled heavy/bulky pickup requiring loading-bay assistance (per the ~40–60 pickups/store/week schedule); the remainder is floor-loaded by customers
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Receiving Clerk, Stock Associate, Customer
Source: workflow W1193 — Heavy &amp; Bulky Material Customer Pickup Scheduling &amp; Loading Bay Priority Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1193_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1193_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1193_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1193_Lane3" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1193_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1193_Start5" name="Customer purchases heavy/bulky items (cement, lumber, plywood, tiles, steel, sand/gravel)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1193_Task6" name="Pickup scheduling at point of sale">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pickup scheduling at point of sale: When customer purchases heavy/bulky items and selects pickup: (a) system checks loading bay availability for the customer&#x27;s preferred date/time, (b) system prompts for vehicle type (pickup truck, multicab, flatbed, van) to plan loading method, (c) system assigns pickup time slot (30-minute windows, max 3 concurrent pickups per store), (d) confirms pickup reservation with QR code sent to customer&#x27;s phone
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1193_Task7" name="Pre-staging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-staging: 30 minutes before customer pickup slot: Stock Associate retrieves heavy items from backroom/lumber yard and stages in designated pickup staging area adjacent to loading bay; cement bags palletized; lumber bundled; tiles on dolly; system updates item status to &quot;Staged for Pickup&quot;
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Receiving Clerk
Duration: 15–30 min/pickup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1193_Task8" name="Customer arrival and verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer arrival and verification: Customer arrives at loading bay at scheduled time; presents QR code; Receiving Clerk scans code to confirm order and items; verifies vehicle type matches reservation; if customer is early or late: Clerk accommodates within ±15 minutes or reschedules if loading bay is occupied
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1193_Task9" name="Loading execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Loading execution: Stock Associate loads materials into customer&#x27;s vehicle with safe loading practices: (a) heavy items first (cement, tiles) on truck bed floor, (b) long items (lumber, rebar) on top or in rack, with red flag for overhang per LTO regulations, (c) weight distributed evenly left-to-right and front-to-back, (d) items secured with rope/straps (provided by store or customer), (e) for quantities exceeding vehicle capacity: advise customer on multiple trips or offer delivery scheduling per W899; forklift used for palletized loads if available
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Receiving Clerk
Duration: 10–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1193_Task10" name="Customer load securing assistance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer load securing assistance: Stock Associate assists customer with securing load: provides tie-down points guidance, offers rope/bungee cords for sale if customer doesn&#x27;t have; for open-bed vehicles carrying cement: covers with tarp (advised, not provided) to prevent moisture damage during transport
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1193_Task11" name="Pickup completion and departure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Pickup completion and departure: System records pickup completion; customer signs electronic Goods Release form; Stock Associate takes photo of loaded vehicle for record; customer departs; loading bay cleared for next pickup
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1193_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1193_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1193_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1193_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: time slot management in Step 1 and separate pickup vs. delivery bay designation where space permits; operational: Stock Associate training on safe loading limits and willingness to refuse unsafe loads; operational: load securing assistance in Step 5 and electronic goods release form documenting customer&#x27;s acceptance of responsibility in Step 6
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1193_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1193_Annotation13" targetRef="W1193_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
