    <bpmn:process id="W_W1272" name="W1272. Store-Level Emergency Local Cash Purchase Authorization &amp; Reimbursement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store encounters urgent need for merchandise or supplies that cannot be fulfilled through standard DC replenishment (W4) or auto-replenishment (W2A) within required timeframe
Frequency: ~2–5 emergency purchases per store per month; ~400–1,000 chain-wide per month
Volume: Typically PHP 500–5,000 per purchase; occasional larger purchases up to PHP 20,000
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Department Supervisor, Receiving Clerk, AP Clerk (HQ)
Source: workflow W1272 — Store-Level Emergency Local Cash Purchase Authorization &amp; Reimbursement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1272_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1272_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1272_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1272_Lane3" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1272_Lane4" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1272_Lane5" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1272_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1272_Start7" name="Store encounters urgent need for merchandise or supplies that cannot be fulfilled through…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task8" name="Emergency need identified">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Emergency need identified: Department Supervisor or Sales Associate identifies urgent need: (a) customer request for out-of-stock item that cannot wait for DC replenishment (trade account customer, large project), (b) critical supply shortage (e.g., cash register receipt paper, cleaning supplies), (c) weather-driven demand surge for specific items; Department Supervisor evaluates urgency: can it wait until next DC delivery (1–3 days)? If no: escalate to Store Manager
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task9" name="Store Manager authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store Manager authorization: Store Manager evaluates emergency purchase request: (a) is the item available at DC? — check real-time inventory (POS-013); if available at DC, expedited replenishment order per W4 is preferred, (b) is the request within authorization limit? — Store Managers authorized up to PHP 5,000 per purchase and PHP 20,000/month cumulative; purchases above PHP 5,000 require Regional Manager phone approval, (c) is the item available from a local supplier at reasonable cost? — Store Manager authorizes purchase or denies (offers customer rain check or backorder per W56)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager (if &gt; PHP 5K)
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task10" name="Local purchase execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Local purchase execution: authorized staff member (typically Department Supervisor or Receiving Clerk) purchases from local supplier: (a) obtain official receipt (OR) or sales invoice from supplier — BIR requirement for reimbursement, (b) pay from petty cash float (PHP 20,000 per store per §10.4) or personal cash (to be reimbursed), (c) select equivalent or identical item — for merchandise, must match BuildRight SKU specification; for supplies, any suitable brand accepted, (d) maximum price: item cost + 20% premium over BuildRight&#x27;s landed cost acceptable for emergency; beyond 20% requires Store Manager re-authorization
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min (travel + purchase)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task11" name="Goods receipt and inventory update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Goods receipt and inventory update: Receiving Clerk processes received goods: (a) for merchandise items — receive into inventory using standard goods receipt per W109, creating receipt against a manually-created emergency PO in the system, (b) for store supplies — receive as non-merchandise with expense category coding, (c) system updates inventory if merchandise, (d) item placed on sales floor or in backroom stock per standard procedure
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task12" name="Documentation and reimbursement request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Documentation and reimbursement request: Store Manager compiles reimbursement documentation: (a) completed emergency purchase form: item description, quantity, supplier name, unit price, total amount, business justification, (b) original BIR-registered receipt/sales invoice from supplier, (c) goods receipt confirmation from step 4, (d) Store Manager signature authorizing reimbursement; documentation submitted to AP (HQ) via system or email within 3 business days of purchase
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task13" name="AP processing and reimbursement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: AP processing and reimbursement: AP Clerk processes reimbursement: (a) verifies documentation completeness — form + original receipt + goods receipt, (b) verifies authorization — Store Manager within limit, Regional Manager if over limit, (c) if petty cash was used: AP replenishes store petty cash float per W541 bank deposit process, (d) if personal cash was used: AP processes employee reimbursement via next payroll cycle (W10) or separate bank transfer, (e) journal entry: debit merchandise inventory (if merchandise) or store supplies expense, credit petty cash or employee reimbursement payable, (f) if supplier is a potential BuildRight vendor, AP flags Category Manager for vendor evaluation per W36
Responsible (R): AP Clerk
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1272_Task14" name="Monthly emergency purchase analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly emergency purchase analysis: Regional Manager reviews monthly emergency purchase reports: (a) frequency by store — stores with &gt; 5 emergency purchases/month flagged for root cause analysis, (b) common items — if same items repeatedly purchased, signal to Supply Planning for ROP/safety stock adjustment per W31, (c) cost premium — total premium paid vs. standard DC cost, (d) petty cash float adequacy — stores consistently exhausting float may need increase
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1272_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1272_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1272_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1272_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: may create duplicate SKUs or incorrect inventory records
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1272_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1272_Annotation16" targetRef="W1272_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
