    <bpmn:process id="W_W1283" name="W1283. Cement &amp; Building Material Vendor Direct Store Delivery (DSD) Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled or ad-hoc vendor DSD delivery of bulky construction materials to store
Frequency: ~2–3 DSD deliveries per store per month; ~500–600 DSD receipts chain-wide per month (per the canon and W1424)
Volume: ~30% of goods by value delivered DSD (cement, lumber, sand, gravel, rebar, hollow blocks)
Owner: Store Receiving Clerk
Participants: Store Receiving Clerk, Department Supervisor, Vendor Driver, Store Manager
Source: workflow W1283 — Cement &amp; Building Material Vendor Direct Store Delivery (DSD) Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1283_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1283_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1283_Lane2" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1283_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1283_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1283_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1283_Start6" name="Scheduled or ad-hoc vendor DSD delivery of bulky construction materials to store">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task7" name="DSD delivery schedule management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DSD delivery schedule management: Department Supervisor maintains weekly DSD delivery calendar per vendor: (a) cement vendors deliver 2–3x/week per store (high consumption), (b) sand/gravel vendors deliver 1–2x/week, (c) lumber/rebar vendors deliver per PO; system sends automated delivery reminders to vendors 24 hours before scheduled delivery; Store Manager reviews schedule for conflicts (multiple DSD trucks arriving simultaneously, limited receiving dock capacity)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task8" name="Pre-delivery preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-delivery preparation: Before scheduled DSD arrival: (a) Receiving Clerk clears designated unloading area (cement storage area, lumber yard, rebar racks), (b) prepares receiving tablet with expected PO details open, (c) ensures forklift or pallet jack is available for heavy items, (d) verifies scale calibration if vendor delivers by weight (sand, gravel), (e) confirms sufficient stock boys available for manual unloading if no dock-level unloading
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task9" name="Vendor arrival &amp; unloading coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor arrival &amp; unloading coordination: Vendor truck arrives; Receiving Clerk: (a) verifies vendor identity and delivery against scheduled PO, (b) directs driver to designated unloading area (cement storage room, lumber yard, or outdoor staging), (c) supervises unloading to ensure proper handling (cement bags not thrown, lumber not dragged, rebar bundles not dropped), (d) for cement: checks bag condition (no torn bags, no hardened cement)
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task10" name="Quantity verification &amp; quality check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quantity verification &amp; quality check: Receiving Clerk performs quantity count: (a) cement: count bags vs. PO quantity (typically delivered in pallets of 40–50 bags), (b) sand/gravel: measure volume (cubic meters) or weight via scale, (c) lumber: count pieces by dimension and length, verify species and grade, (d) rebar: count bundles and verify diameter/length; quality checks: (e) cement: no lumps or moisture damage (squeeze test), (f) hollow blocks: check for cracks, verify dimensions, (g) rebar: check for excessive rust
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task11" name="Goods receipt posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Goods receipt posting: Receiving Clerk posts goods receipt in ERP via handheld tablet: (a) select PO, (b) enter received quantity per line, (c) note any discrepancies (short shipment, over-shipment, damaged items), (d) capture vendor delivery receipt photo for 3-way match per W7, (e) system updates store inventory in real-time and triggers AP invoice matching
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task12" name="Discrepancy resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Discrepancy resolution: If quantity discrepancy or quality issue: (a) Receiving Clerk notes on vendor delivery receipt and takes photos, (b) both Receiving Clerk and vendor driver sign annotated delivery receipt, (c) Department Supervisor notified for items &gt;10% variance or quality rejection, (d) for quality rejection: vendor driver takes back rejected items; system records rejected quantity, (e) for quantity variance: post goods receipt for accepted quantity only; AP adjusts PO per actual per W7
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task13" name="DSD storage &amp; staging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: DSD storage &amp; staging: Receiving Clerk directs stock associates to place goods in designated storage: (a) cement: indoor storage on pallets (never directly on floor — moisture wicking), stacked max 10 bags high, rotated FIFO (older stock at front), (b) sand/gravel: dumped in designated outdoor bin, (c) hollow blocks: stacked in yard area, (d) rebar: placed in steel racks by diameter; system updates storage location for inventory visibility
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1283_Task14" name="Monthly DSD vendor performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly DSD vendor performance tracking: Store Manager compiles monthly DSD vendor scorecard data: (a) on-time delivery rate, (b) quantity accuracy, (c) quality rejection rate, (d) driver cooperation and unloading efficiency; feeds into vendor performance management per W44; flags vendors with chronic issues to Category Manager for sourcing review per W36
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1283_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1283_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1283_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1283_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-261 (ensure controlled execution — Store Receiving &amp; Replenishment (PA-07.3).) | - operational: per W440
Owner: Store Receiving Clerk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1283_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1283_Annotation16" targetRef="W1283_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1283_Flow18" sourceRef="W1283_Start6" targetRef="W1283_Task7" />
